   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription With Ajit Agarkar departing his role as the chief selector of the Indian men’s cricket team, Pragyan Ojha now leads a reconstituted five-member selection committee. With the 2027 ODI World Cup on the horizon, how much power do Indian cricket selectors really have? In this episode of In Focus, we discuss about Agarkar’s legacy, what to expect from Ojha at the helm, and how selectors build and blood a squad.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。随着阿吉特·阿加尔卡卸任印度男子板球队首席选拔员，普拉金·奥贾如今领导一个经过重组的五人选拔委员会。2027年ODI世界杯近在眼前，印度板球选拔员究竟拥有多大权力？在《聚焦》本期节目中，我们讨论阿加尔卡的legacy、奥贾执掌选拔委员会后的期待，以及选拔员如何组建并检验球队阵容。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription With Ajit Agarkar departing his role as the chief selector of the Indian men’s cricket team, Pragyan Ojha now leads a reconstituted five-member selection committee. With the 2027 ODI World Cup on the horizon, how much power do Indian cricket selectors really have? In this episode of In Focus, we discuss about Agarkar’s legacy, what to expect from Ojha at the helm, and how selectors build and blood a squad. We also discuss how much say the captain and the coach have, how the scouting network covers India’s enormous domestic talent pool, and whether selectors should explain their decisions in public. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
