   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The most riveting days of cricket in the Ranji Trophy are those where the contest keeps oscillating like a pendulum among the two teams. The second day of the Elite Group-C clash between Delhi and Services at the Airforce Complex Ground in Palam was very much like that, but Ayush Doseja (78, 154b, 6x4) and Sumit Mathur (80 n.o. The sixth-wicket partnership between the two left-handers was worth 144 runs as Delhi reached 299 for six at close of play on Tuesday.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后解锁这些内容。拉吉杯赛最精彩的比赛日，是两队之间的胜负像钟摆一样反复摇摆的日子。德里队与驻军队在帕拉姆空军基地进行的精英组C组对决第二日便呈现这种局面，但阿尤什·多塞贾（78分，154球，6个四分）和苏米特·马苏尔（80分，未出局出局）表现出色。两位左手击球手之间的第六 partnerships  partnerships 价值144分，帮助德里队在周二比赛结束时以299分、6人出局收场。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The most riveting days of cricket in the Ranji Trophy are those where the contest keeps oscillating like a pendulum among the two teams. The second day of the Elite Group-C clash between Delhi and Services at the Airforce Complex Ground in Palam was very much like that, but Ayush Doseja (78, 154b, 6x4) and Sumit Mathur (80 n.o. 159b, 8x4, 2x6) ensured that the host had its nose in front by the end. The sixth-wicket partnership between the two left-handers was worth 144 runs as Delhi reached 299 for six at close of play on Tuesday. Ayush Badoni & Co. are 33 runs in the green after bundling out Services for 266 on the opening day. Since entering the set-up, Doseja and Mathur have displayed a propensity for consistency with the bat. Here too, they were desperately needed after the side was reduced to 135 for five in 39.2 overs. Both batters did enjoy some luck. Mathur was dropped on nought by Pulkit Narang at gully off 21-year-old pacer Jayant Goyat. Doseja was on 42 when Narang created a chance with his off-spin, but Ravi Chauhan spilled the catch at short-leg. But it wouldn’t have mattered as much if Doseja and Mathur hadn’t capitalised in the manner that they did. Having done the hard work, Doseja would have certainly liked to catch further attention with a three-figure score, but Virender Nepal had the No. 5 batter caught down the leg side in the 87th over. For Services, the breakthroughs were spread among four bowlers. Left-arm tweaker Arjun Sharma got the well-set Priyansh Arya (58, 88b, 1x4, 3x6) to hole out at long-off. Badoni, who had hit double tons in his last two games, was castled by the spinner whilst attempting a slog sweep. Goyat also struck twice even as Narang and Virender snared a wicket each. Delhi / national championship / national tournament / sport / sports event / domestic Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
