   "title": "Melania Trump to Host Russian and Ukrainian Delegations at White House",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/03/melania-trump-to-host-russian-and-ukrainian-delegations-at-white-house-a94165",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Tue, 03 Nov 2026 17:25:00 +0300",
   "_dt": 1793715900.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "U.S. first lady Melania Trump will host representatives from Russia and Ukraine at the White House this week to deliver remarks on a recently concluded ceasefire and humanitarian mission in the occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky, the White House announced Tuesday. “This achievement marks an unprecedented diplomatic initiative by an American First Lady,” the White House said in a statement, adding that Melania Trump will deliver an address on the Oleshky ceasefire at 11 a.m. Eastern Time on Thursday.",
   "summary_zh": "白宫周二宣布，美国第一夫人梅拉尼娅·特朗普本周将在白宫接待俄罗斯和乌克兰的代表，就 recently 达成的停火协议以及在乌克兰被占领城镇奥列什基开展的人道主义任务发表讲话。白宫在声明中表示：“这一成就标志着美国第一夫人开展了一项前所未有的外交行动。”梅拉尼娅·特朗普将于周四美国东部时间上午11时就奥列什基停火协议发表讲话。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "U.S. first lady Melania Trump will host representatives from Russia and Ukraine at the White House this week to deliver remarks on a recently concluded ceasefire and humanitarian mission in the occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky, the White House announced Tuesday. The six-day ceasefire, which ended Sunday, had allowed emergency aid to reach Oleshky and any civilians to leave if they wanted, either to Ukrainian-controlled territory or Russia. “This achievement marks an unprecedented diplomatic initiative by an American First Lady,” the White House said in a statement, adding that Melania Trump will deliver an address on the Oleshky ceasefire at 11 a.m. Eastern Time on Thursday. It did not name the Russian and Ukrainian representatives invited to appear during the address. A Ukrainian official told The Kyiv Independent that Russian Human Rights Commissioner Yana Lantratova and her Ukrainian counterpart Dmytro Lubinets will attend the White House event. Lantratova is currently under U.S. sanctions and will need a sanctions waiver from the State Department to enter the country. The announcement follows a report in the French newspaper Le Monde that claimed the humanitarian operation in Oleshky was negotiated over the course of four months by Russia’s GRU and Ukraine’s HUR military intelligence agencies. Sources cited by the newspaper suggested that Russia and Ukraine had agreed to credit the first lady for the ceasefire as a way to placate U.S. President Donald Trump as he seeks a diplomatic breakthrough in peace negotiations. Russia and the U.S. confirmed this week that trilateral talks aimed at ending the war in Ukraine will resume in Abu Dhabi on Nov. 10 and 11 after having stalled in February due to the conflict in the Middle East. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ru"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_moscowtimes",
   "title_zh": "梅拉尼娅·特朗普将在白宫接待俄罗斯和乌克兰代表团",
   "body_zh": "美国第一夫人梅拉尼娅·特朗普本周将在白宫接待俄罗斯和乌克兰的代表，就不久前结束的停火协议以及在乌克兰被占城市奥列什基实施的 humanitarian 任务发表讲话。白宫周二宣布了这一消息。这场为期六天的停火协议于周日结束，期间紧急援助得以送达奥列什基，任何愿意离开的平民也可以前往乌克兰控制区或俄罗斯。白宫在一份声明中表示：“这一成果标志着美国第一夫人发起了一项前所未有的外交行动。”声明补充说，梅拉尼娅·特朗普将于周四东部时间上午11时就奥列什基停火协议发表讲话。声明没有说明获邀在讲话期间出席的俄罗斯和乌克兰代表姓名。一名乌克兰官员告诉《基辅独立报》，俄罗斯人权事务专员雅娜·兰特拉托娃和乌克兰人权事务专员德米特罗·卢比涅茨将出席白宫活动。兰特拉托娃目前受到美国制裁，进入美国前需要获得美国国务院的豁免。此前，法国《世界报》报道称，奥列什基的人道主义行动是俄罗斯GRU和乌克兰HUR军事情报机构在四个月内协商达成的。该报引述的消息人士称，俄罗斯和乌克兰同意将这次停火归功于美国第一夫人，以此安抚正在寻求和平谈判取得外交突破的美国总统唐纳德·特朗普。俄罗斯和美国本周证实，旨在结束乌克兰战争的三方会谈将于11月10日和11日在阿布扎比恢复。此前会谈因中东冲突于2月陷入停滞。我们正面临前所未有的挑战。俄罗斯总检察长办公室已将《莫斯科时报》认定为“不受欢迎”组织，将我们的工作定性为犯罪，使我们的员工面临被起诉的风险。此前，我们还曾被不公正地标记为“外国代理人”。这些行动是直接企图压制俄罗斯的独立新闻业。当局声称我们的工作“诋毁俄罗斯领导层的决定”。我们却有不同看法：我们致力于提供有关俄罗斯的准确、不偏不倚的报道。我们《莫斯科时报》的记者拒绝噤声。但要继续我们的工作，我们需要您的帮助。您的支持无论多么微小，都会带来翻天覆地的变化。如果可以，请从每月2美元开始支持我们。设置起来很快，每一笔捐款都会产生重大影响。支持《莫斯科时报》，就是在镇压面前捍卫开放、独立的新闻业。感谢您与我们站在一起",
