   "summary": "The Ghana Chamber of Clean Energy (GCCE) has identified seven major financing constraints affecting businesses in Ghana's electric two-wheeler industry, warning that the challenges could limit the sector's growth. The workshop brought together electric two-wheeler manufacturers, assemblers, retailers, financial institutions and other industry stakeholders to examine financing barriers and explore ways to improve access to capital.",
   "summary_zh": "加纳清洁能源商会（GCCE）确定了影响加纳电动两轮车行业企业的七项主要融资障碍，并警告称，这些挑战可能限制该行业的发展。此次研讨会汇聚了电动两轮车制造商、组装商、零售商、金融机构及行业其他利益相关方，共同审视融资障碍，并探讨改善资本获取渠道的办法。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The Ghana Chamber of Clean Energy (GCCE) has identified seven major financing constraints affecting businesses in Ghana's electric two-wheeler industry, warning that the challenges could limit the sector's growth. The concerns were outlined at a stakeholder consultative workshop organised by GCCE in partnership with the William Davidson Institute (WDI) at the University of Michigan in Accra on Tuesday, October 27, 2026. The workshop brought together electric two-wheeler manufacturers, assemblers, retailers, financial institutions and other industry stakeholders to examine financing barriers and explore ways to improve access to capital. A research team working with the two organisations presented seven preliminary financing gaps identified through the study. These include the limited implementation of announced import duty waivers for electric two-wheeler businesses and difficulties tran",
