   "title": "2027: Egba Group Rejects INEC’s Alleged Selective Enforcement of Supreme Court Decision",
   "url": "https://www.thisdaylive.com/2026/11/03/2027-egba-group-rejects-inecs-alleged-selective-enforcement-of-supreme-court-decision/",
   "domain": "thisdaylive.com",
   "source": "ThisDay（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 03 Nov 2026 02:32:06 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793673126.0,
   "ageDays": 0.53,
   "summary": "Egba Integrity Group (EIG) condemned what it called selective enforcement of the law by the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) following the commission’s meeting of Thursday, October 29. The group said INEC enforced the Supreme Court’s decision on the timeline for submission of political parties’ membership registers in the case of governorship candidates, but refused to do same for the National Assembly candidates in Ogun State.",
   "summary_zh": "Egba Integrity Group（EIG）谴责独立国家选举委员会（INEC）选择性执法。EIG称，INEC在10月29日星期四的会议之后，遵守了最高法院关于州长候选人所属政党提交党员名册时限的裁决，却拒绝对奥贡州国民议会候选人适用同样规定。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Egba Integrity Group (EIG) condemned what it called selective enforcement of the law by the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) following the commission’s meeting of Thursday, October 29. The group said INEC enforced the Supreme Court’s decision on the timeline for submission of political parties’ membership registers in the case of governorship candidates, but refused to do same for the National Assembly candidates in Ogun State. It added, “The Supreme Court on September 24, 2026 in INEC v ZLP SC/CV/495/2026 held that Section 77(5)(6)(7) Electoral Act 2026 is mandatory. The group insisted that what INEC did on October 29 was selective enforcement. It stated, “For governorship: INEC enforced strictly – Isa Pantami (PDP Gombe) – cleared conditionally, Abdulsalam Gwarzo (NDC Kano), cleared conditionally, and Ladi Adebutu (PDP Ogun Gov), rejected. “INEC said ‘The Ogun PDP candidate did not succeed. For National Assembly, INEC refused to enforce same. PDP Ogun defective register that disqualified Adebutu was used to retain Sen. Iyabo Obasanjo (PDP Ogun Central) and other National Assembly candidates. That is illegal discrimination. “Section 77 does not distinguish between Governor and Senate. The register is one. If register is invalid for governor, it is invalid for Senate.” Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
