   "title": "Gold mining formalisation must not legitimise environmental destruction",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/gold-mining-formalisation-must-not-legitimise-environmental-destruction-clgb/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:02:02 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793624522.0,
   "ageDays": 1.09,
   "summary": "The Chamber of Licensed Gold Buyers (CLGB) has urged the government to adopt a conditional and evidence-based approach to formalising Ghana’s artisanal and small-scale mining (ASM) sector, warning against granting legitimacy to operations that cause environmental destruction. The Chamber says the GoldBod-led formalisation programme presents an opportunity to address longstanding challenges in the sector through an accessible, transparent and enforceable regulatory framework.",
   "summary_zh": "持牌黄金买家商会（CLGB）敦促政府采取有条件、以证据为基础的方式，推动加纳手工采矿和小规模采矿（ASM）行业正规化，并警告不要赋予那些造成环境破坏的采矿活动合法地位。该商会表示，由加纳黄金局主导的正规化计划，为通过易于参与、透明且可执行的监管框架解决该行业长期存在的问题提供了机会。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The Chamber of Licensed Gold Buyers (CLGB) has urged the government to adopt a conditional and evidence-based approach to formalising Ghana’s artisanal and small-scale mining (ASM) sector, warning against granting legitimacy to operations that cause environmental destruction. The Chamber says the GoldBod-led formalisation programme presents an opportunity to address longstanding challenges in the sector through an accessible, transparent and enforceable regulatory framework. However, in a policy statement, it stressed that government must distinguish between mining operations that can be conducted lawfully and responsibly and those that threaten water bodies, forests, agricultural lands and public health",
   "bodyLevel": "excerpt",
