   "title": "20 jawans martyred in Galwan.",
   "url": "https://x.com/morning_star_ar/status/2117247392504574144",
   "snippet": "20 jawans martyred in Galwan. And what did we get? “Na koi ghusa hai, na koi ghusa hua hai.” 🙂\nSix years later:\n– Arunachal: ITBP’s own DG says confrontations with Chinese troops are “continuing at multiple locations.” PLA tents reportedly pitched 6–7 km inside India’s side of the LAC.\n– Assam: China is building the world’s largest dam on the Brahmaputra, Assam’s lifeline, right next to our border. Our response? “Monitoring.”\n– Meanwhile, Xi Jinping was hosted in India last month like an old friend, handshakes and photo-ops.\n56 inch ka seena only for opposition leaders, students and comedians. For China, it’s “dialogue,” “normalisation” and silence.\nMark my words: the man who sold himself as Mr Strongman will be remembered as the PM who blinked at Beijing. Desh ki suraksha pe compromise, aur voter bhoolta nahi. 🇮🇳🔥",
   "body": "20 jawans martyred in Galwan. And what did we get? “Na koi ghusa hai, na koi ghusa hua hai.” 🙂\nSix years later:\n– Arunachal: ITBP’s own DG says confrontations with Chinese troops are “continuing at multiple locations.” PLA tents reportedly pitched 6–7 km inside India’s side of the LAC.\n– Assam: China is building the world’s largest dam on the Brahmaputra, Assam’s lifeline, right next to our border. Our response? “Monitoring.”\n– Meanwhile, Xi Jinping was hosted in India last month like an old friend, handshakes and photo-ops.\n56 inch ka seena only for opposition leaders, students and comedians. For China, it’s “dialogue,” “normalisation” and silence.\nMark my words: the man who sold himself as Mr Strongman will be remembered as the PM who blinked at Beijing. Desh ki suraksha pe compromise, aur voter bhoolta nahi. 🇮🇳🔥",
