   "title": "In October, shipments of Russian oil from Baltic and Arctic seas ports to China via Northern Sea Route continued Launch of Vostok‑Oil became",
   "url": "https://x.com/seala_ai/status/2116967254814290431",
   "snippet": "In October, shipments of Russian oil from Baltic and Arctic seas ports to China via Northern Sea Route continued\n\nLaunch of Vostok‑Oil became a key factor in the growth of shipments along the eastern route of Northern Sea Route this year.\n\nUsing the Arctic route for supplies from the Baltic reduces the voyage time to China by half (from 51 days from Ust‑Luga to Qingdao around the Cape of Good Hope to 27 days via the Northern Sea Route). \n\nEven seasonal use of NSR helps to improve economy of Russian crude oil exports. At the same time, navigation through the Bering Strait will be closed in November and flows will be reset.\n\n#NothernSeaRoute #Arctic #oil #SealaTerminal\n @seala_ai",
   "body": "In October, shipments of Russian oil from Baltic and Arctic seas ports to China via Northern Sea Route continued\n\nLaunch of Vostok‑Oil became a key factor in the growth of shipments along the eastern route of Northern Sea Route this year.\n\nUsing the Arctic route for supplies from the Baltic reduces the voyage time to China by half (from 51 days from Ust‑Luga to Qingdao around the Cape of Good Hope to 27 days via the Northern Sea Route). \n\nEven seasonal use of NSR helps to improve economy of Russian crude oil exports. At the same time, navigation through the Bering Strait will be closed in November and flows will be reset.\n\n#NothernSeaRoute #Arctic #oil #SealaTerminal\n @seala_ai",
