   "platform": "x",
   "title": "🚨 TRENDING TODAY: NPF 48HR OPERATIONAL SUCCESSES 🚨 Kindly find below the Top 15 State-by-State Executive Summary of @policeNG Operational Su",
   "url": "https://x.com/CspIniedu/status/2116789283813982261",
   "snippet": "🚨 TRENDING TODAY: NPF 48HR OPERATIONAL SUCCESSES 🚨\n\nKindly find below the Top 15 State-by-State Executive Summary of @policeNG Operational Successes for the last 48 hours:\n\n1. ZAMFARA STATE: POLICE ENGAGEMENT FORCES BANDITS TO ABANDON FIVE ABDUCTED WOMEN\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 1230HRS, armed bandits attacked a farm in Dansadau, Maru LGA, shot dead a 35-year-old farmer, and abducted five elderly women harvesting beans.\n✅ Police tactical teams and local vigilantes pursued the assailants and engaged them in a gun duel, forcing the bandits to abandon all five captives and flee.\n✅ All five abducted women were rescued unhurt, while sustained bush-combing and tracking operations continue to apprehend the perpetrators.\n🔹 Status: SCID Gusau Investigating.\n\n2. NIGER STATE: JOINT RESCUE OPERATION FREES SIX ABDUCTED FARMERS\n✅ On 29/10/2026, police, military, DSS, special hunters and local vigilantes traced armed bandits to their hideout in Rafi LGA.\n✅ The coordinated operation successfully rescued six victims abducted while working on their farms at Mahangi Village via Pandogari.\n✅ The rescued victims were received at the Division for profiling ahead of reunion with their relatives.\n🔹 Status: SCID Minna Investigating.\n\n3. KEBBI STATE: JOINT SECURITY FORCES THWART LAKURAWA ATTACK ON RIBAH\n✅ On 30/10/2026 at about 2015HRS, armed men suspected to be bandits attacked Ribah Town, Danko Wasagu LGA, after an earlier attempt to block Rambo Junction was thwarted by joint security forces.\n✅ The attackers regrouped and opened fire from different directions, prompting joint forces to engage them and repel the attack.\n🔹 Status: SCID Birnin Kebbi Investigating.\n\n4. KANO STATE: POLICE ARREST FIVE SUSPECTS, RECOVER 48 COWS, 43 SHEEP AND TWO MOTORCYCLES\n✅ Police Anti-Kidnapping Squad operatives stormed the residence of suspects linked to the kidnapping of Alh. Abdu Fanka, APC Chairman of Rogo LGA.\n✅ Although the primary suspects escaped after raising an alarm, operatives arrested five persons suspected of harbouring criminals.\n✅ Police recovered 48 cows, 43 sheep and two Bajaj Boxer motorcycles during the operation.\n🔹 Status: SCID Bompai Investigating.\n\n5. KATSINA STATE: POLICE FOIL ARMED BANDITS' ATTACK ON KAROFI VILLAGE\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 2327HRS, tactical teams responded to a distress call concerning an attempted bandit attack on Karofi Village, Dutsin-Ma LGA.\n✅ Police operatives intercepted the hoodlums and engaged them in a gun duel, forcing the attackers to abandon their mission and retreat into the bush.\n✅ No casualty was recorded among security personnel or civilians, while combined patrols and bush-combing operations continue.\n🔹 Status: SCID Katsina Investigating.\n\n6. LAGOS STATE: POLICE ARREST CULTIST SUSPECT AFTER ARMED ROBBERY/MURDER, RECOVER FIREARM\n✅ On 31/10/2026 at about 1130HRS, police operatives responded swiftly to an ongoing robbery at Desa Bus Stop, Ibeju-Lekki.\n✅ Operatives arrested Ojo/Ojomu Bolanle, 28, aka “Burna”, a suspected Aiye confraternity member, following the shooting of POS operator Ibrahim Adewale Moronfade, who later died.\n✅ A search led to the recovery of one locally-made pistol, one expended cartridge and charms, while the stolen handbag and other property were traced to the robbery.\n🔹 Status: SCID Panti Investigating.\n\nCSP ANI INIEDU, anipr\nFORCE PUBLIC RELATIONS OFFICER\nLOUIS EDET HOUSE\nFORCE HEADQUARTERS\nABUJA\n\n#PoliceIsYourFriend #CitizensAreTheBoss\n#NPFOperationalSuccesses #PoliceNG\n#SaferNigeria #EndViolentCrimes\n#NigeriaPolice #CrimePrevention\n#RescueMission #CounterTerrorism\n#CommunityPolicing\n@TunjiDisu1 @PoliceNG @MobilePunch @SaharaReporters @vanguardngrnews @daily_trust @GuardianNigeria @DailyPostNGR @TheNationNews @PremiumTimesng @PulseNigeria247 @THISDAYLIVE @tvcnewsng @channelstv @AIT_Online @ARISEtv @NTANewsNow",
   "body": "🚨 TRENDING TODAY: NPF 48HR OPERATIONAL SUCCESSES 🚨\n\nKindly find below the Top 15 State-by-State Executive Summary of @policeNG Operational Successes for the last 48 hours:\n\n1. ZAMFARA STATE: POLICE ENGAGEMENT FORCES BANDITS TO ABANDON FIVE ABDUCTED WOMEN\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 1230HRS, armed bandits attacked a farm in Dansadau, Maru LGA, shot dead a 35-year-old farmer, and abducted five elderly women harvesting beans.\n✅ Police tactical teams and local vigilantes pursued the assailants and engaged them in a gun duel, forcing the bandits to abandon all five captives and flee.\n✅ All five abducted women were rescued unhurt, while sustained bush-combing and tracking operations continue to apprehend the perpetrators.\n🔹 Status: SCID Gusau Investigating.\n\n2. NIGER STATE: JOINT RESCUE OPERATION FREES SIX ABDUCTED FARMERS\n✅ On 29/10/2026, police, military, DSS, special hunters and local vigilantes traced armed bandits to their hideout in Rafi LGA.\n✅ The coordinated operation successfully rescued six victims abducted while working on their farms at Mahangi Village via Pandogari.\n✅ The rescued victims were received at the Division for profiling ahead of reunion with their relatives.\n🔹 Status: SCID Minna Investigating.\n\n3. KEBBI STATE: JOINT SECURITY FORCES THWART LAKURAWA ATTACK ON RIBAH\n✅ On 30/10/2026 at about 2015HRS, armed men suspected to be bandits attacked Ribah Town, Danko Wasagu LGA, after an earlier attempt to block Rambo Junction was thwarted by joint security forces.\n✅ The attackers regrouped and opened fire from different directions, prompting joint forces to engage them and repel the attack.\n🔹 Status: SCID Birnin Kebbi Investigating.\n\n4. KANO STATE: POLICE ARREST FIVE SUSPECTS, RECOVER 48 COWS, 43 SHEEP AND TWO MOTORCYCLES\n✅ Police Anti-Kidnapping Squad operatives stormed the residence of suspects linked to the kidnapping of Alh. Abdu Fanka, APC Chairman of Rogo LGA.\n✅ Although the primary suspects escaped after raising an alarm, operatives arrested five persons suspected of harbouring criminals.\n✅ Police recovered 48 cows, 43 sheep and two Bajaj Boxer motorcycles during the operation.\n🔹 Status: SCID Bompai Investigating.\n\n5. KATSINA STATE: POLICE FOIL ARMED BANDITS' ATTACK ON KAROFI VILLAGE\n✅ On 29/10/2026 at about 2327HRS, tactical teams responded to a distress call concerning an attempted bandit attack on Karofi Village, Dutsin-Ma LGA.\n✅ Police operatives intercepted the hoodlums and engaged them in a gun duel, forcing the attackers to abandon their mission and retreat into the bush.\n✅ No casualty was recorded among security personnel or civilians, while combined patrols and bush-combing operations continue.\n🔹 Status: SCID Katsina Investigating.\n\n6. LAGOS STATE: POLICE ARREST CULTIST SUSPECT AFTER ARMED ROBBERY/MURDER, RECOVER FIREARM\n✅ On 31/10/2026 at about 1130HRS, police operatives responded swiftly to an ongoing robbery at Desa Bus Stop, Ibeju-Lekki.\n✅ Operatives arrested Ojo/Ojomu Bolanle, 28, aka “Burna”, a suspected Aiye confraternity member, following the shooting of POS operator Ibrahim Adewale Moronfade, who later died.\n✅ A search led to the recovery of one locally-made pistol, one expended cartridge and charms, while the stolen handbag and other property were traced to the robbery.\n🔹 Status: SCID Panti Investigating.\n\nCSP ANI INIEDU, anipr\nFORCE PUBLIC RELATIONS OFFICER\nLOUIS EDET HOUSE\nFORCE HEADQUARTERS\nABUJA\n\n#PoliceIsYourFriend #CitizensAreTheBoss\n#NPFOperationalSuccesses #PoliceNG\n#SaferNigeria #EndViolentCrimes\n#NigeriaPolice #CrimePrevention\n#RescueMission #CounterTerrorism\n#CommunityPolicing\n@TunjiDisu1 @PoliceNG @MobilePunch @SaharaReporters @vanguardngrnews @daily_trust @GuardianNigeria @DailyPostNGR @TheNationNews @PremiumTimesng @PulseNigeria247 @THISDAYLIVE @tvcnewsng @channelstv @AIT_Online @ARISEtv @NTANewsNow",
